.KEY demo
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; Where the GL chain stops, and how long each link takes.
;
; ISSUE-0045 records a machine that does not come back from the first GL
; program. Two explanations were open -- stuck, or crawling through a 10 MB
; library on a JIT that has to translate every block once -- and neither can
; be told from the other by a probe that only says "running glinfo".
;
; So each link is opened on its own, with the clock either side. Everything
; goes to DEBUG: so it survives a machine that stops answering: a stop with no
; output and a stop after a known line are different findings.
;
; Version <name> opens the library. That is the point: the cost is the load,
; the relocation and the init, not the version string.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-probe] libraries present:"
List >DEBUG: LIBS:gl.library LIBS:gallium.library LIBS:mesa3dgl20-0.library
Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-probe] drivers present:"
List >DEBUG: DEVS:Drivers/gallium.hidd DEVS:Drivers/vc4gallium.hidd DEVS:Drivers/softpipe.hidd

Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-probe] --- opening gallium.library"
Date >DEBUG:
Version >DEBUG: gallium.library
Date >DEBUG:

Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-probe] --- opening mesa3dgl20-0.library (10 MB)"
Date >DEBUG:
Version >DEBUG: mesa3dgl20-0.library
Date >DEBUG:

Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-probe] --- opening gl.library"
Date >DEBUG:
Version >DEBUG: gl.library
Date >DEBUG:

Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-probe] --- running glinfo"
Date >DEBUG:
SYS:Extras/Demos/GL/glinfo >DEBUG:
Date >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-probe] glinfo returned"
